"name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v10.0.9\n\n- (@krobipd) Fixed: a table with `encryptedAttributes` showed the stored secrets still encrypted and encrypted them a second time on the next save, so the adapter could no longer decrypt them. Since 8.5.0 the rows were only decrypted when the attribute was empty (`||=` instead of `&&=`); they are decrypted again when set, and a table stored as an object (`objKeyName`) no longer throws there\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: the same table decrypted its rows directly in the live configuration instead of in a copy. That encryption is a simple XOR, so a second pass turns a secret back into plain text: switching a tab remounts the table and encrypted the shown secrets again, and saving any other field wrote the table secrets unencrypted into the instance object. The rows are decrypted in a copy now, as the save path already did. A secret that a table stored this way since 8.5.0 should be entered once again","tree":{"sha":"61b1a994da146e7736b47d135ec96c39c803d0aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/git/trees/61b1a994da146e7736b47d135ec96c39c803d0aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/git/commits/4ce022b83060ef34c0b6d95fb21fe29d18524e85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanB