vatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/commits/b7be652aca47e1eef20aeae6ac66e546d40cab9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:45:13Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:45:13Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v10.0.7\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: a `selectSendTo` with `multiple: true` could not be used when the adapter answers with numeric values (`{ label: ''Heat'', value: 9 }`). The checkbox of a menu item compared the value as text but stored it as a number, so it never appeared as checked and every click added the entry again instead of removing it - the configuration filled up with duplicates. The comparison is tolerant about the type now, which also repairs a configuration that was written this way, and the entries are sorted as numbers instead of as text (ioBroker.admin#3636)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Fixed: in the same component, clicking a checkbox and clicking the text of a menu item disagreed about where the value lives. After the first click on a checkbox, selecting an item by its text no longer changed anything visible, because the rendered list was frozen on the internal state while only the data behind it changed","tree":{"sha":"01cd67873be4c416f1139834e91056c11387a1f3","url":"https://api.github.com