ha":"dff3d577041e5caf043b4822f8e85449d9585351","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/commits/dff3d577041e5caf043b4822f8e85449d9585351"}],"sha":"528873af2969d358d45f897e2a1d8c12419643ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/commits/528873af2969d358d45f897e2a1d8c12419643ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/commits/dff3d577041e5caf043b4822f8e85449d9585351/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:10:39Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:10:39Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v10.0.0\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) The schema allows the root property `command` of a JSON tab now. It was documented and honoured by admin, but every `jsonTab.json5` that uses it was reported as invalid: https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.admin/issues/3610\n- (@GermanBluefox) The schema of `divider` accepts any CSS color and a height as a CSS length, as the control has always rendered them. Until now only `primary`/`secondary` and a number were allowed\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added `ack` to the `state` control: the value is written as a command (`ack: false`) by default, as before, and an adapter that only shows its own value can now ask for an acknowledged write\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added `highlight` to the `state` control, which highlights the line on mouse over, like `staticInfo` already did\n- (@GermanBluefox) **Breaking for hosts:** `react-ace` is not a dependency of this library anymore. The host hands the editor in with the new property `AceEditor` of `JsonConfig` / `JsonConfigComponent`, together with the modes `json`, `json5`, `yaml` and the themes `clouds_midnight`, `chrome`. Without it the editors are plain text areas. Until now every bundle that uses this library carried the whole `ace-builds` along, the custom components of all adapters included","tree":{"sha":"1eb6014eb3eb86cebdb7ec2aa74909c0c3bae327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/git/trees/1eb6014eb3eb86cebdb7ec2aa74909c0c3bae327"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/json-config/git/commits/dff3d577041e5caf043b4822f8e85449d9585351","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_e