pshot retrieval and ping functionality.\n- Added TypeScript definitions for registered plugins to ensure type safety.\n- Developed unit tests for the DataProviderService, validating snapshot structure and response data.\n- Configured TypeScript build settings and Vitest configurations for unit and integration testing.\n\n* fix contract\n\n* fixed the across, lifi, layer zero and axelar plugins and created the cbridge implementation. (#21)\n\n* clean\n\n* feat: add Li.Fi bridge data adapter for NEAR Intents (#18)\n\n- Li.Fi adapter with comprehensive data collection\n- Real-time rates, liquidity depth, and volume metrics\n- Chunked volume fetching with v2/v1 fallback strategy\n- Rate limiting compliance (700ms delays, 20 RPM limit)\n- Binary search liquidity probing for 50bps/100bps thresholds\n- Robust error handling and fallback mechanisms\n- Full test coverage (unit + integration tests)\n- Live demo verified: 6M+ 30d volume, 3M 24h volume\n- Contract compliance: oRPC getSnapshot & ping procedures\n\n* updated debridge plugin - wali (#13)\n\n* fix wali\n\n* add cbridge\n\n* update assessments\n\n* alignment\n\n* update\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ussyalfaks <usmanalfaki@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: 0xJesus <pdlgmcn@protonmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Posma Janius Sianturi <posma2018@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Wali <humaidwali20@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f05d6ab815a1b962f4126a04ac1b92ea9a96931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Psianturi/lifi-adapter-for-near/git/trees/6f05d6ab815a1b962f4126a04ac1b92ea9a96931"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Psianturi/lifi-adapter-for-near/git/commits/849bac1799d7937d908c1884f5240b1904d841da","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f05d6ab815a1b962f4126a04ac1b92ea9a96931\nparent 972ba03afbd34d0ce8734d9674d134aa1f7166cc\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1762896470 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1762896470 -0700\n\nAdds all plugins for review with assessment (#12)\n\n* add all repos\n\n* adds missing wormhole 0xjesus plugin\n\n* adds and partially converts all plugins\n\n* full migration\n\n* standardize ports and add to api\n\n* fix\n\n* add assessments\n\n* assessments\n\n* feat: Add Axelar Plugin Test Suite and Integration Tests\n\n- Created a new HTML file for testing the Axelar Plugin API with various endpoints.\n- Implemented integration tests for the Data Provider Plugin using Vitest, covering snapshot retrieval and ping functionality.\n- Added TypeScript definitions for registered plugins to ensure type safety.\n- Developed unit tests for the DataProviderService, validating snapshot structure and response data.\n- Configured TypeScript build settings and Vitest configurations for unit and integration testing.\n\n* fix contract\n\n* fixed the across, lifi, layer zero and axelar plugins and created the cbridge implementation. (#21)\n\n* clean\n\n* feat: add Li.Fi bridge data adapter for NEAR Intents (#18)\n\n- Li.Fi adapter with comprehensive data collection\n- Real-time rates, liquidity depth, and volume metrics\n- Chunked volume fetching with v2/v1 fallback strategy\n- Rate limiting compliance (700ms delays, 20 RPM limit)\n- Binary search liquidity probing for 50bps/100bps thresholds\n- Robust error handling and fallback mechanisms\n- Full test coverage (unit + integration tests)\n- Live demo verified: 6M+ 30d volume, 3M 24h volume\n- Contract compliance: oRPC getSnapshot & ping procedures\n\n* updated debridge plugin - wali (#13)\n\n* fix wali\n\n* add cbridge\n\n* update assessments\n\n* alignment\n\n* update\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ussyalfaks <usmanalfaki@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: 0xJesus <pdlgmcn@protonmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Posma Janius Sianturi <posma2018@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Wali <humaidwali20@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpE6pWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA228QAKgxt0UNGZYb90VMYjGiOhlL\nyh5bBOcwh+7qqhnNdPjH1Dx1JJU05kZvA19gfrkhd/g3+B4l2qn3w3a4MUrO8nsT\nw/DmcpVhIfIE/VIWb+A6s5quyNxlzojakpRYSj