api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/commits/0166a242cae4b41d627b472b72c197131c96c7e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-29T03:17:27Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-29T03:17:27Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"message":"feat: Add test coverage for ChatWidget component\n\nThis commit introduces test coverage for the `ChatWidget` component and resolves issues in the Jest test environment.\n\nKey changes include:\n- **Test Environment Fix:** Configured Jest and Babel to correctly handle ES Module dependencies from libraries like `@privy-io/react-auth` and `ethers`. This was achieved by adding a `babel.config.js` with the `next/babel` preset and updating `jest.config.cjs` to use `babel-jest`.\n- **Polyfill:** Added a polyfill for `TextEncoder` and `TextDecoder` in `jest.setup.cjs` to support dependencies that rely on these browser APIs.\n- **ChatWidget Tests:** Created a new test suite for the `ChatWidget` component (`components/__tests__/ChatWidget.test.js`). The tests cover rendering with initial props, user input, and asynchronous message sending by mocking the `fetch` API.\n- **Gitignore:** Added the `coverage/` directory to `.gitignore` to exclude test coverage reports from version control.","tree":{"sha":"ab0bfe126acddd78ce1eaae670d2df77460788c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/git/trees/ab0bfe126acddd78ce1eaae670d2df77460788c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/git/commits/0166a242cae4b41d627b472b72c197131c96c7e1","verificat