"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/commits/f339c8a8062f9c1656895b5328bb4ea92b3f6cf0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-27T12:55:56Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-27T12:55:56Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"message":"feat: Implement IaC Agent Sync Logic (Phase 1)\n\nThis commit introduces the core backend functionality for managing AI agents as code. It includes:\n\n- A new `agents:sync` npm script to synchronize local agent definitions with the Nation platform.\n- A module (`src/lib/iac`) containing the logic for loading, mapping, and diffing agent definitions.\n- The script handles both the creation of new agents (including auto-updating the source file with the remote address) and the updating of existing agents by detecting differences.\n- The entire flow is testable via a mock API client included in the script.\n\nThis completes the backend and CLI deliverables for Phase 1 of the IaC feature.","tree":{"sha":"fa206fa4af7b49c4eab4172a34e7d307feacf5f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/git/trees/fa206fa4af7b49c4eab4172a34e7d307feacf5f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/git/commits/f339c8a8062f9c1656895b5328bb4ea92b3f6cf0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/842251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_u