hub.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/commits/b5c3833f70098f6d0d8a9d2c8bf307cbe0705668/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-27T00:06:34Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-27T00:06:34Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"message":"fix(ci): Ensure test report directory exists before running tests\n\nThis commit fixes a bug in the CI workflow where the test artifact was not being generated, causing the deployment workflow to fail with an \"Artifact not found\" error.\n\nThe root cause was that the ''cucumber-js'' test runner does not automatically create the output directory for its JSON report. If the ''reports/'' directory did not exist, the report generation would fail silently.\n\nThis change adds a ''mkdir -p reports'' step to the ''ci.yml'' workflow before the tests are run, ensuring the directory always exists. This guarantees that the test report is generated and uploaded as an artifact, allowing the subsequent deployment workflow to succeed.","tree":{"sha":"f6bcf95a62379d735b3580f0861e9aebc4281125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/git/trees/f6bcf95a62379d735b3580f0861e9aebc4281125"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govinda777/nation.fun/git/commits/b5c3833f70098f6d0d8a9d2c8bf307cbe0705668","verific